    {
      "id": "syn_interpretive_questions_7ae0aa175816",
      "kind": "interpretive_questions",
      "facts": [
        "This evidence explains why barriers and priestly duties are integral to holiness and approach rather than arbitrary decoration.",
        "The court, outer room, inner room, veils, washing, and differentiated personnel form a graded system of access; assigning an independent symbolic meaning to every measurement, color, or material exceeds what Exodus explains.",
        "Ancient parallels demonstrate possible forms of mobile elite or sacred space, but no Mari text, Egyptian relief, Timna phase, or bark shrine is the biblical tabernacle or proves direct dependence.",
        "At Timna Site 200, a New Kingdom Egyptian Hathor shrine was followed by a materially different phase in which post holes and textile remains have been interpreted as a tented cult installation.",
        "Timna supplies a geographically and chronologically relevant example of cult space incorporating tent material while providing no evidence that it was Israel's dwelling or followed Exodus's plan."
      ],
      "verse_refs": [
        "Exodus 26:1-37",
        "Exodus 26:31-37"
      ],
