    {
      "id": "syn_interpretive_questions_8405255f90ed",
      "kind": "interpretive_questions",
      "facts": [
        "No excavated structure can presently be identified as the wilderness tabernacle described in Exodus; Timna Site 200 is a different shrine with a disputed later-phase interpretation.",
        "Exodus and Numbers portray a sanctuary constructed from transportable components, dismantled and carried by assigned personnel, and re-erected within Israel's camp.",
        "An Old Babylonian Mari administrative text concerning a large tent installation supplies evidence that substantial public tents could carry political or ritual significance.",
        "The Mari text makes a large socially important tent culturally intelligible without providing the plan, cult, chronology, or identity of Exodus's dwelling."
      ],
      "verse_refs": [
        "Exodus 26:1-37"
      ],
